{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-36009" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the gradient of $g(x,y)$ at the point $(\\frac{1}{2},0)$ if $g(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-36009" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\ {g}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{2y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the gradient is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇g(x,y) & =⟨{g}_{x}(x,y),\\,{g}_{y}(x,y)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}},\\,\\frac{2y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}⟨x,\\,y⟩ \\\\ ∇g(\\frac{1}{2},\\,0) & =\\frac{2}{{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+{0}^{2}}⟨\\frac{1}{2},\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\,\\frac{1}{4}}⟨\\frac{1}{2},\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =8⟨\\frac{1}{2},\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-36009" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "868401a7f37e42bd10de04419ec5ed8ed954a846d1b4a3b0a48d8334dfc0160d"} {"question" "q-36009" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-36009" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨4,\\,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨8,\\,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨8,\\,\\frac{1}{2}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{1}{2},\\,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{1}{2},\\,\\frac{1}{2}⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-36009" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨4,\\,0⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-127650" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $h(x,y)=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x}),$ find $∇h(x,y).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-127650" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the partial derivatives: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+{(\\frac{y}{x})}^{2}}\\cdot (-\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\cdot (-\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+{(\\frac{y}{x})}^{2}}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =-\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,i+\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-127650" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "868401a7f37e42bd10de04419ec5ed8ed954a846d1b4a3b0a48d8334dfc0160d"} {"question" "q-127650" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-127650" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,i+\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,j"] ["math" "-\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,i+\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,j"] ["math" "-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,i+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,j"] ["math" "\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,i-\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,j"] ["math" "\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,i-\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,j"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-127650" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,i+\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,j"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-36909" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate $∇f(x,y)$ at $(2,1)$ if $f(x,y)={x}^{2}\\sqrt{y+3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-36909" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}\\sqrt{y+3}) \\\\  & =2x\\sqrt{y+3} \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}\\sqrt{y+3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2\\sqrt{y+3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the gradient is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =⟨{f}_{x}(x,y),\\,{f}_{y}(x,y)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2x\\sqrt{y+3},\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2\\sqrt{y+3}}⟩ \\\\ ∇f(2,1) & =⟨2\\cdot 2\\sqrt{1+3},\\,\\frac{{2}^{2}}{2\\sqrt{1+3}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-36909" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "868401a7f37e42bd10de04419ec5ed8ed954a846d1b4a3b0a48d8334dfc0160d"} {"question" "q-36909" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-36909" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨1,\\,8⟩"] ["math" "⟨16,\\,1⟩"] ["math" "⟨2,\\,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨4,\\,\\frac{1}{2}⟩"] ["math" "⟨8,\\,1⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-36909" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨8,\\,1⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-36910" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given  $g(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2})$, find $∇g(x,y).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-36910" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{xy}\\cdot y+0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {g}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{xy}\\cdot x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})\\cdot 2y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{y}-2y\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the gradient is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇g(x,y) & ={g}_{x}(x,y)\\text{ }i+{g}_{y}(x,y)\\text{ }j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}\\text{ }i+(\\frac{1}{y}-2y\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2}))\\text{ }j\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-36910" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "868401a7f37e42bd10de04419ec5ed8ed954a846d1b4a3b0a48d8334dfc0160d"} {"question" "q-36910" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-36910" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{x}\\text{ }i+(\\frac{1}{y}+2y\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)\\text{ }j"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{x}\\text{ }i+(\\frac{1}{y}-2y\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2}))\\text{ }j"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{x}\\text{ }i+2y(\\frac{1}{y}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2}))\\text{ }j"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{x}\\text{ }i+\\frac{1}{y}\\text{ }j"] ["math" "x\\text{ }i+(y-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2}))\\text{ }j"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-36910" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{x}\\text{ }i+(\\frac{1}{y}-2y\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2}))\\text{ }j"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-36005" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate $∇h(x,y)$ at $(1,1)$ if $h(x,y)=4x\\operatorname{arctan}⁡y.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-36005" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the partial derivatives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4x\\operatorname{arctan}⁡y) \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{arctan}⁡y \\\\ {h}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4x\\operatorname{arctan}⁡y) \\\\  & =\\frac{4x}{{y}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the gradient is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇h(x,y) & =⟨{h}_{x}(x,y),\\,{h}_{y}(x,y)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4\\operatorname{arctan}⁡y,\\,\\frac{4x}{{y}^{2}+1}⟩ \\\\ ∇h(1,1) & =⟨4\\operatorname{arctan}⁡1,\\,\\frac{4\\cdot 1}{{1}^{2}+1}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4},\\,\\frac{4}{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\pi ,\\,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-36005" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "868401a7f37e42bd10de04419ec5ed8ed954a846d1b4a3b0a48d8334dfc0160d"} {"question" "q-36005" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-36005" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨1,\\,1⟩"] ["math" "⟨2\\pi ,\\,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\,\\frac{1}{2}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\pi ,\\,2⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\pi ,\\,\\frac{1}{2}⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-36005" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨\\pi ,\\,2⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-71422" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given $h(x,y,z)=xy\\operatorname{ln}⁡(z)$, find $∇h(x,y,z).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-71422" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}_{x}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy\\operatorname{ln}⁡(z)) \\\\  & =y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(z) \\\\ {h}_{y}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy\\operatorname{ln}⁡(z)) \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(z) \\\\ {h}_{z}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xy\\operatorname{ln}⁡(z)) \\\\  & =xy\\cdot \\frac{1}{z} \\\\  & =\\frac{xy}{z}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the gradient is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇h(x,y,z) & ={h}_{x}(x,y,z)\\text{ }i+{h}_{y}(x,y,z)\\text{ }j+{h}_{z}(x,y,z)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(z)\\text{ }i+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(z)\\text{ }j+\\frac{xy}{z}\\text{ }k\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-71422" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "868401a7f37e42bd10de04419ec5ed8ed954a846d1b4a3b0a48d8334dfc0160d"} {"question" "q-71422" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-71422" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(z)\\text{ }i+y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(z)\\text{ }j+xy\\operatorname{ln}⁡(z)\\text{ }k"] ["math" "xy\\operatorname{ln}⁡(z)\\text{ }i+xy\\operatorname{ln}⁡(z)\\text{ }j+\\frac{xy}{z}\\text{ }k"] ["math" "y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(yz+zx)\\text{ }i+y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(yz+zx)\\text{ }j+\\frac{xy}{z}\\text{ }k"] ["math" "y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(z)\\text{ }i+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(z)\\text{ }j+\\frac{xy}{z}\\text{ }k"] ["math" "y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(z)\\text{ }i+xy\\text{ }j+\\frac{xy}{z}\\text{ }k"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-71422" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(z)\\text{ }i+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(z)\\text{ }j+\\frac{xy}{z}\\text{ }k"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-36918" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given $f(x,y,z)=\\sqrt{xyz}$, find $∇f(x,y,z).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-36918" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\sqrt{xyz}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{xyz}}\\cdot (yz) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{xyz}}{2x} \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{xyz}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{xyz}}\\cdot (xz) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{xyz}}{2y} \\\\ {f}_{z}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\sqrt{xyz}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{xyz}}\\cdot (xy) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{xyz}}{2z}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the gradient is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\text{ }i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\text{ }j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{xyz}}{2x}\\text{ }i+\\frac{\\sqrt{xyz}}{2y}\\text{ }j+\\frac{\\sqrt{xyz}}{2z}\\text{ }k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{xyz}}{2}(\\frac{1}{x}\\text{ }i+\\frac{1}{y}\\text{ }j+\\frac{1}{z}\\text{ }k)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-36918" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "868401a7f37e42bd10de04419ec5ed8ed954a846d1b4a3b0a48d8334dfc0160d"} {"question" "q-36918" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-36918" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{xyz}}{2}(\\frac{1}{x}\\text{ }i+\\frac{1}{y}\\text{ }j+\\frac{1}{z}\\text{ }k)"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{xyz}}{2}(x\\text{ }i+y\\text{ }j+z\\text{ }k)"] ["math" "\\frac{xyz}{2}(\\frac{1}{x}\\text{ }i+\\frac{1}{y}\\text{ }j+\\frac{1}{z}\\text{ }k)"] ["math" "\\sqrt{xyz}(\\frac{1}{yz}\\text{ }i+\\frac{1}{xz}\\text{ }j+\\frac{1}{xz}\\text{ }k)"] ["math" "\\sqrt{xyz}(x\\text{ }i+y\\text{ }j+z\\text{ }k)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-36918" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{xyz}}{2}(\\frac{1}{x}\\text{ }i+\\frac{1}{y}\\text{ }j+\\frac{1}{z}\\text{ }k)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-36969" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate $∇f(x,y,z)$ at the point $(2,3,1)$ if $f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt{xyz}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-36969" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt{xyz})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{xyz}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{xyz}}\\cdot yz \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2x} \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt{xyz})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{xyz}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{xyz}}\\cdot xz \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2y} \\\\ {f}_{z}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt{xyz})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{xyz}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{xyz}}\\cdot xy \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2z}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\text{ }i+{f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\text{ }j+{f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2x}\\text{ }i+\\frac{1}{2y}\\text{ }j+\\frac{1}{2z}\\text{ }k \\\\ ∇f(2,3,1) & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 2}\\text{ }i+\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 3}\\text{ }j+\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 1}\\text{ }k \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\text{ }i+\\frac{1}{6}\\text{ }j+\\frac{1}{2}\\text{ }k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-36969" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "868401a7f37e42bd10de04419ec5ed8ed954a846d1b4a3b0a48d8334dfc0160d"} {"question" "q-36969" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-36969" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "4\\text{ }i+6\\text{ }j-2\\text{ }k"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}\\text{ }i+\\frac{1}{3}\\text{ }j+k"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}\\text{ }i+\\frac{1}{3}\\text{ }j-k"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}\\text{ }i+\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6}\\text{ }j-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\text{ }k"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}\\text{ }i+\\frac{1}{6}\\text{ }j+\\frac{1}{2}\\text{ }k"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-36969" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{4}\\text{ }i+\\frac{1}{6}\\text{ }j+\\frac{1}{2}\\text{ }k"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-71425" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $∇g(x,y,z)$ given that  $g(x,y,z)={x}^{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+{e}^{xyz}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-71425" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{x}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+{e}^{xyz}) \\\\  & =2x{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+yz{e}^{xyz} \\\\ {g}_{y}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+{e}^{xyz}) \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}y{z}^{2}+xz{e}^{xyz} \\\\ {g}_{z}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+{e}^{xyz}) \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}{y}^{2}z+xy{e}^{xyz}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,  the gradient is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇g(x,y,z) & ={g}_{x}(x,y,z)\\text{ }i+{g}_{y}(x,y,z)\\text{ }j+{g}_{z}(x,y,z)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =(2x{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+yz{e}^{xyz})\\text{ }i+(2{x}^{2}y{z}^{2}+xz{e}^{xyz})\\text{ }j+(2{x}^{2}{y}^{2}z+xy{e}^{xyz})\\text{ }k\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-71425" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "868401a7f37e42bd10de04419ec5ed8ed954a846d1b4a3b0a48d8334dfc0160d"} {"question" "q-71425" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-71425" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(2x+yz{e}^{xyz})\\text{ }i+(2y+xz{e}^{xyz})\\text{ }j+(2z+xy{e}^{xyz})\\text{ }k"] ["math" "(2x{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+x{e}^{xyz})\\text{ }i+(2{x}^{2}y{z}^{2}+y{e}^{xyz})\\text{ }j+(2{x}^{2}{y}^{2}z+z{e}^{xyz})\\text{ }k"] ["math" "(2x{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+yz{e}^{xyz})\\text{ }i+(2{x}^{2}y{z}^{2}+xz{e}^{xyz})\\text{ }j+(2{x}^{2}{y}^{2}z+xy{e}^{xyz})\\text{ }k"] ["math" "(2x{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+{e}^{xyz})\\text{ }i+(2{x}^{2}y{z}^{2}+{e}^{xyz})\\text{ }j+(2{x}^{2}{y}^{2}z+{e}^{xyz})\\text{ }k"] ["math" "(x{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+yz{e}^{xyz-1})\\text{ }i+({x}^{2}y{z}^{2}+xz{e}^{xyz-1})\\text{ }j+({x}^{2}{y}^{2}z+xy{e}^{xyz-1})\\text{ }k"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-71425" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(2x{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+yz{e}^{xyz})\\text{ }i+(2{x}^{2}y{z}^{2}+xz{e}^{xyz})\\text{ }j+(2{x}^{2}{y}^{2}z+xy{e}^{xyz})\\text{ }k"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-36968" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $∇g(x,y,z)$ given that  $g(x,y,z)=\\sqrt{x+2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt{yz}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-36968" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{x}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\sqrt{x+2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt{yz})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+2}}+0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+2}} \\\\ {g}_{y}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{x+2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt{yz})) \\\\  & =0+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{yz}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{yz}}\\cdot z \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2y} \\\\ {g}_{z}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\sqrt{x+2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt{yz})) \\\\  & =0+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{yz}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{yz}}\\cdot y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2z}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,  the gradient is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇g(x,y,z) & ={g}_{x}(x,y,z)\\text{ }i+{g}_{y}(x,y,z)\\text{ }j+{g}_{z}(x,y,z)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+2}}i+\\frac{1}{2y}\\text{ }j+\\frac{1}{2z}\\text{ }k\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-36968" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "868401a7f37e42bd10de04419ec5ed8ed954a846d1b4a3b0a48d8334dfc0160d"} {"question" "q-36968" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-36968" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+2}}i+\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{y}}\\text{ }j+\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{z}}\\text{ }k"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+2}}i+\\frac{1}{2yz}\\text{ }j+\\frac{1}{2yz}\\text{ }k"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+2}}i+\\frac{1}{2y}\\text{ }j+\\frac{1}{2z}\\text{ }k"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x+2}}i+\\frac{1}{yz}\\text{ }j+\\frac{1}{yz}\\text{ }k"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x+2}}i+\\frac{1}{y}\\text{ }j+\\frac{1}{z}\\text{ }k"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-36968" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+2}}i+\\frac{1}{2y}\\text{ }j+\\frac{1}{2z}\\text{ }k"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-128517" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $f(x,y)={x}^{2}-2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y,$ find the points $(x,y),$ for $0\\le y<\\pi ,$ where $∇f(x,y)=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-128517" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}-2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y) \\\\  & =2x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡y \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}-2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y) \\\\  & =2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $∇f(x,y)=2(x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)\\,i+2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,j.$\n\nNow, we solve $∇f(x,y)=0:$ \n\n$$\n2(x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)\\,i+2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,j=0\\text{ }i+0\\text{ }j\n$$\n\nSo, by equating the coefficients of $i$ and $j,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2(x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)=0 \\\\ 2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get $x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡y.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\operatorname{sin}⁡y & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡2y & =0 \\\\ y & =0,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $y=0,$ we get $x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡0=1.$\n\n- For $y=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ we get $x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=0.$\n\nTherefore, $∇h(x,y)=0,$ for $0\\le y<\\pi ,$ at two points: $(1,0)$ and $(0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-128517" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "868401a7f37e42bd10de04419ec5ed8ed954a846d1b4a3b0a48d8334dfc0160d"} {"question" "q-128517" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-128517" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$(-1,0)$ and $(1,\\frac{\\pi }{2})$"] ["text" "$(0,\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ only"] ["text" "$(1,0)$ and $(0,\\frac{\\pi }{2})$"] ["text" "$(1,0)$ only"] ["text" "$(1,\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-128517" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$(1,0)$ and $(0,\\frac{\\pi }{2})$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-128519" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $g(x,y)=\\frac{9}{y}-\\frac{3y}{x}+x,$ find the points $(x,y)$ where $∇g(x,y)=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-128519" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{9}{y}-\\frac{3y}{x}+x) \\\\  & =\\frac{3y}{{x}^{2}}+1 \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{9}{y}-\\frac{3y}{x}+x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{{y}^{2}}-\\frac{3}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $∇g(x,y)=(\\frac{3y}{{x}^{2}}+1)i-(\\frac{9}{{y}^{2}}+\\frac{3}{y})j.$\n\nNow, we solve $∇g(x,y)=0:$\n\n$$\n(\\frac{3y}{{x}^{2}}+1)i-(\\frac{9}{{y}^{2}}+\\frac{3}{x})j=0\\,i+0\\,j\n$$\n\nSo, by equating the coefficients of $i$ and $j,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3y}{{x}^{2}}+1=0 \\\\ \\frac{9}{{y}^{2}}+\\frac{3}{x}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get $y=-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9}{{(-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3})}^{2}}+\\frac{3}{x} & =0 \\\\ 9\\cdot {(-\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}})}^{2}+\\frac{3}{x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{81}{{x}^{4}}+\\frac{3}{x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{81+3{x}^{3}}{{x}^{4}} & =0 \\\\ 81+3{x}^{3} & =0 \\\\ {x}^{3} & =-27 \\\\ x & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=-3,$ we get $y=-\\frac{(-3)^{2}}{3}=-3.$\n\nTherefore, $∇g(x,y)=0$ at the point: $(-3,-3).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-128519" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "868401a7f37e42bd10de04419ec5ed8ed954a846d1b4a3b0a48d8334dfc0160d"} {"question" "q-128519" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-128519" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$(-3,-3)$ only"] ["text" "$(-3,3)$ only"] ["text" "$(3,-3)$ and $(-3,3)$"] ["text" "$(3,3)$ and $(-3,-3)$"] ["text" "$(3,3)$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-128519" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$(-3,-3)$ only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-35995" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $f(x,y)=3{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-x$, find the points $(x,y)$ where $∇f(x,y)=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-35995" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-x) \\\\  & =6x+0-1 \\\\  & =6x-1 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-x) \\\\  & =0+2y-0 \\\\  & =2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $∇f(x,y)=(6x-1)\\,i+2y\\,j.$\n\nNow, we solve $∇f(x,y)=0:$\n\n$$\n(6x-1)\\,i+2y\\,j=0\\text{ }i+0\\text{ }j\n$$\n\nSo, by equating the coefficients of $i$ and $j,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}6x-1=0 \\\\ 2y=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get $x=\\frac{1}{6}.$ From the second equation, we obtain $y=0.$ \n\nTherefore, $∇f(x,y)=0$ at the point $(\\frac{1}{6},0)\\,.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-35995" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "868401a7f37e42bd10de04419ec5ed8ed954a846d1b4a3b0a48d8334dfc0160d"} {"question" "q-35995" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-35995" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(0,0)"] ["math" "(0,\\frac{1}{2})"] ["math" "(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{12})"] ["math" "(\\frac{1}{6},0)"] ["math" "(\\frac{1}{6},\\frac{1}{2})"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-35995" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(\\frac{1}{6},0)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-71474" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{1}{xy}+\\frac{1}{y}+\\frac{1}{zx}-z$, find the points $(x,y,z)$ where $∇f(x,y,z)=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-71474" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the partial derivatives: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{1}{xy}+\\frac{1}{y}+\\frac{1}{zx}-z) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}y}+0-\\frac{1}{z{x}^{2}}-0 \\\\  & =-\\frac{z+y}{{x}^{2}yz} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{1}{xy}+\\frac{1}{y}+\\frac{1}{zx}-z) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{x{y}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}+0-0 \\\\  & =-\\frac{1+x}{x{y}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\frac{1}{xy}+\\frac{1}{y}+\\frac{1}{zx}-z) \\\\  & =0+0-\\frac{1}{{z}^{2}x}-1 \\\\  & =-\\frac{1+{z}^{2}x}{{z}^{2}x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $∇f(x,y,z)=-\\frac{z+y}{{x}^{2}yz}\\,i-\\frac{1+x}{x{y}^{2}}\\,j-\\frac{1+{z}^{2}x}{{z}^{2}x}\\,k.$ \n\nNow, we solve $∇f(x,y,z)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{z+y}{{x}^{2}yz}\\,i-\\frac{1+x}{x{y}^{2}}\\,j-\\frac{1+{z}^{2}x}{{z}^{2}x}\\,k & =0\\text{ }i+0\\text{ }j+0\\text{ }j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by equating the coefficient of $i$, $j$, and $k$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{z+y}{{x}^{2}yz}=0 \\\\ -\\frac{1+x}{x{y}^{2}}=0 \\\\ -\\frac{1+{z}^{2}x}{{z}^{2}x}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get $x=-1.$ Substituting these into the third equation, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1+{z}^{2}x}{{z}^{2}x} & =0 \\\\ -\\frac{1+{z}^{2}(-1)}{{z}^{2}(-1)} & =0 \\\\ 1-{z}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {z}^{2} & =1 \\\\ z & =\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-1$ into the first equation, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{z+y}{(-1)^{2}yz} & =0 \\\\ z+y & =0 \\\\ y & =-z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen $z=1,$ we have $y=-1$ and when $z=-1,$ we have $y=1.$\n\nHence, $∇f(x,y,z)=0$ at two points: $(-1,-1,1)$ and $(-1,1,-1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-71474" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "868401a7f37e42bd10de04419ec5ed8ed954a846d1b4a3b0a48d8334dfc0160d"} {"question" "q-71474" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-71474" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$(-1,-1,-1)$ and $(-1,1,1)$"] ["text" "$(-1,-1,1)$ and $(-1,1,-1)$"] ["text" "$(-1,-1,1)$ only"] ["text" "$(-1,1,-1)$ only"] ["text" "$(1,-1,-1)$ and $(1,1,1)$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-71474" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$(-1,-1,1)$ and $(-1,1,-1)$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-36970" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given $h(x,y,z)=xy+x{y}^{2}+{z}^{3}.$ Find the points $(x,y,z)$ where $∇h(x,y,z)=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-36970" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}_{x}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy+x{y}^{2}+{z}^{3}) \\\\  & =y+{y}^{2}+0 \\\\  & =y+{y}^{2} \\\\ {h}_{y}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy+x{y}^{2}+{z}^{3}) \\\\  & =x+2xy+0 \\\\  & =x+2xy \\\\ {h}_{z}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xy+x{y}^{2}+{z}^{3}) \\\\  & =0+0+3{z}^{2} \\\\  & =3{z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $∇h(x,y,z)=(y+{y}^{2})\\,i+(x+2xy)\\,j+3{z}^{2}\\,k.$\n\nNow, we solve $∇f(x,y,z)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+{y}^{2})\\,i+(x+2xy)\\,j+3{z}^{2}\\,k & =0\\text{ }i+0\\text{ }j+0\\text{ }j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by equating the coefficients of $i$, $j$, and $k$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y+{y}^{2}=0 \\\\ x+2xy=0 \\\\ 3{z}^{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe first equation can be written as $y(1+y)=0$, which gives $y=0$ or $y=-1.$ Substituting these into the second equation, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2x(0) & =0 \\\\ x & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nor,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2x(-1) & =0 \\\\ x & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, from the third equation, we get $z=0.$\n\nTherefore, $∇h(x,y,z)=0$ at two points: $(0,0,0)$ and $(0,-1,0).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-36970" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "868401a7f37e42bd10de04419ec5ed8ed954a846d1b4a3b0a48d8334dfc0160d"} {"question" "q-36970" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-36970" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$(0,-1,0)$ only"] ["text" "$(0,0,0)$ and  $(-1,-1,-1)$"] ["text" "$(0,0,0)$ and $(0,-1,0)$"] ["text" "$(0,0,0)$ only"] ["text" "$(1,-1,1)$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-36970" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$(0,0,0)$ and $(0,-1,0)$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-71476" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the gradient of the product $f(x,y)h(x,y),$ given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & ={x}^{2}y+x{y}^{2},\\, &  & ∇f(x,y)=(2xy+{y}^{2})\\text{ }i+({x}^{2}+2xy)\\text{ }j, &  &  \\\\ h(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{xy},\\, &  & ∇h(x,y)=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}y}\\text{ }i-\\frac{1}{x{y}^{2}}\\text{ }j. &  & \\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-71476" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The gradient of the product of two functions $f(x,y)$ and $h(x,y)$ is given by:\n\n$$\n∇[fh]=h\\,∇\\,f+f\\,∇\\,h\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇[f(x,y)h(x,y)] & =h(x,y)∇f(x,y)+f(x,y)∇h(x,y) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{xy}((2xy+{y}^{2})\\text{ }i+({x}^{2}+2xy)\\text{ }j)+({x}^{2}y+x{y}^{2})(-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}y}\\text{ }i-\\frac{1}{x{y}^{2}}\\text{ }j) \\\\  & =(\\frac{2xy+{y}^{2}}{xy}\\text{ }i+\\frac{{x}^{2}+2xy}{xy}\\text{ }j)+(-\\frac{{x}^{2}y+x{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}y}\\text{ }i-\\frac{{x}^{2}y+x{y}^{2}}{x{y}^{2}}\\text{ }j) \\\\  & =(\\frac{2x+y}{x}\\text{ }i+\\frac{x+2y}{y}\\text{ }j)+(-\\frac{x+y}{x}\\text{ }i-\\frac{x+y}{y}\\text{ }j) \\\\  & =(-\\frac{x+y}{x}+\\frac{2x+y}{x})\\text{ }i+(-\\frac{x+y}{y}+\\frac{x+2y}{y})\\text{ }j \\\\  & =\\text{ }i+\\text{ }j\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-71476" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "868401a7f37e42bd10de04419ec5ed8ed954a846d1b4a3b0a48d8334dfc0160d"} {"question" "q-71476" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-71476" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\text{ }i+\\text{ }j"] ["math" "\\text{ }i+\\text{ }j"] ["math" "\\text{ }i-\\text{ }j"] ["math" "x\\text{ }i+y\\text{ }j"] ["math" "y\\text{ }i+x\\text{ }j"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-71476" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\text{ }i+\\text{ }j"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-65131" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the gradient of the product $f(x,y)g(x,y),$ given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =xy,\\, &  & ∇f(x,y)=y\\text{ }i+x\\text{ }j, &  &  \\\\ g(x,y) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy),\\, &  & ∇g(x,y)=\\frac{1}{x}\\text{ }i+\\frac{1}{y}\\text{ }j. &  & \\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-65131" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The gradient of the product of two functions $f(x,y)$ and $g(x,y)$ is given by:\n\n$$\n∇[fg]=g\\,∇\\,f+f\\,∇\\,g\n$$\n\nSo, using this product rule we obtain: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇[f(x,y)g(x,y)] & =g(x,y)∇f(x,y)+f(x,y)∇g(x,y) \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy))(y\\text{ }i+x\\text{ }j)+xy(\\frac{1}{x}\\text{ }i+\\frac{1}{y}\\text{ }j) \\\\  & =y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)\\text{ }i+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)\\text{ }j+y\\text{ }i+x\\text{ }j \\\\  & =[y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)\\text{ }i+y\\text{ }i]+[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)\\text{ }j+x\\text{ }j] \\\\  & =y(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)+1)\\text{ }i+x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)+1)\\text{ }j\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-65131" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "868401a7f37e42bd10de04419ec5ed8ed954a846d1b4a3b0a48d8334dfc0160d"} {"question" "q-65131" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-65131" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)\\text{ }i+y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)\\text{ }j"] ["math" "x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)\\text{ }i-y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)\\text{ }j"] ["math" "y(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)+1)\\text{ }i+x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)+1)\\text{ }j"] ["math" "y(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)+2)\\text{ }i+x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)+2)\\text{ }j"] ["math" "y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)\\text{ }i+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)\\text{ }j"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-65131" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)+1)\\text{ }i+x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)+1)\\text{ }j"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-128521" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the gradient of the product $f(x,y)g(x,y)$ if $f(x,y)=x{y}^{2}$ and $g(x,y)={e}^{-({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-128521" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The gradient of the product of two functions $f(x,y)$ and $g(x,y)$ is given by\n\n$$\n∇[fg]=f∇g+g∇f.\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the partial derivatives of $f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x{y}^{2})={y}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{y}^{2})=2xy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\text{ }j={y}^{2}\\text{ }i+2xy\\text{ }j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the partial derivatives of $g(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{-({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})})=-2x{e}^{-({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})} \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{-({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})})=-2y{e}^{-({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇g(x,y) & =\\frac{∂g}{∂x}\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\text{ }j=-2x{e}^{-({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}\\text{ }i-2y{e}^{-({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}\\text{ }j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the product rule, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇[f(x,y)g(x,y)] & =x{y}^{2}(-2x{e}^{-({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}\\text{ }i-2y{e}^{-({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}\\text{ }j)+{e}^{-({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}({y}^{2}\\text{ }i+2xy\\text{ }j) \\\\  & ={e}^{-({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}(-2{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\text{ }i-2x{y}^{3}\\text{ }j)+{e}^{-({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}({y}^{2}\\text{ }i+2xy\\text{ }j) \\\\  & ={e}^{-({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}({y}^{2}(1-2{x}^{2})\\text{ }i+2xy(1-{y}^{2})\\text{ }j).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-128521" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "868401a7f37e42bd10de04419ec5ed8ed954a846d1b4a3b0a48d8334dfc0160d"} {"question" "q-128521" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-128521" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{e}^{-({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}(x(1-{y}^{2})\\text{ }i+xy(1-{x}^{2})\\text{ }j)"] ["math" "{e}^{-({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}(y(1-2{x}^{2})\\text{ }i+x(1+2{y}^{2})\\text{ }j)"] ["math" "{e}^{-({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}({x}^{2}(1+{y}^{2})\\text{ }i+2{y}^{2}(1+{x}^{2})\\text{ }j)"] ["math" "{e}^{-({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}({y}^{2}(1-2{x}^{2})\\text{ }i+2xy(1-{y}^{2})\\text{ }j)"] ["math" "{e}^{-({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}({y}^{2}(1-{x}^{2})\\text{ }i+2xy(1-{y}^{2})\\text{ }j)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-128521" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{e}^{-({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}({y}^{2}(1-2{x}^{2})\\text{ }i+2xy(1-{y}^{2})\\text{ }j)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-36144" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the gradient of the product $g(x,y)h(x,y),$ given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(x,y) & =3{x}^{2}-4y,\\, &  & ∇g(x,y)=6x\\text{ }i-4\\text{ }j, &  &  \\\\ h(x,y) & =2{x}^{2}{y}^{2},\\, &  & ∇h(x,y)=4x{y}^{2}\\text{ }i+4{x}^{2}y\\text{ }j. &  & \\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-36144" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The gradient of the product of two functions $g(x,y)$ and $h(x,y)$ is given by:\n\n$$\n∇[gh]=h\\,∇\\,g+g\\,∇\\,h\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇[g(x,y)h(x,y)] & =h(x,y)∇g(x,y)+g(x,y)∇h(x,y) \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}{y}^{2}(6x\\text{ }i-4\\text{ }j)+(3{x}^{2}-4y)(4x{y}^{2}\\text{ }i+4{x}^{2}y\\text{ }j) \\\\  & =(2{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\cdot 6x\\text{ }i-2{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\cdot 4\\text{ }j)+((3{x}^{2}-4y)\\cdot 4x{y}^{2}\\text{ }i+(3{x}^{2}-4y)\\cdot 4{x}^{2}y\\text{ }j) \\\\  & =12{x}^{3}{y}^{2}\\text{ }i-8{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\text{ }j+(12{x}^{3}{y}^{2}-16x{y}^{3})\\text{ }i+(12{x}^{4}y-16{x}^{2}{y}^{2})\\text{ }j \\\\  & =(24{x}^{3}{y}^{2}-16x{y}^{3})\\text{ }i+(12{x}^{4}y-24{x}^{2}{y}^{2})\\text{ }j\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-36144" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "868401a7f37e42bd10de04419ec5ed8ed954a846d1b4a3b0a48d8334dfc0160d"} {"question" "q-36144" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-36144" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(12{x}^{4}y-24{x}^{2}{y}^{2})\\text{ }i+(24{x}^{3}{y}^{2}-16x{y}^{3})\\text{ }j"] ["math" "(24{x}^{3}{y}^{2}-16x{y}^{3})\\text{ }i+(12{x}^{4}y-24{x}^{2}{y}^{2})\\text{ }j"] ["math" "(2{x}^{3}{y}^{2}-x{y}^{3})\\text{ }i+({x}^{4}y-2{x}^{2}{y}^{2})\\text{ }j"] ["math" "-16x{y}^{3}\\text{ }i+12{x}^{4}y\\text{ }j"] ["math" "24{x}^{3}{y}^{2}-16x{y}^{3}+12{x}^{4}y-24{x}^{2}{y}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-36144" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(24{x}^{3}{y}^{2}-16x{y}^{3})\\text{ }i+(12{x}^{4}y-24{x}^{2}{y}^{2})\\text{ }j"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-128529" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the gradient of the product $f(x,y,z)h(x,y,z),$ given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =x{y}^{2}{z}^{3},\\, &  & ∇f(x,y,z)={y}^{2}{z}^{3}\\,i+2xy{z}^{3}\\,j+3x{y}^{2}{z}^{2}\\,k, &  &  \\\\ h(x,y,z) & =\\frac{1}{xyz},\\, &  & ∇h(x,y,z)=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}yz}\\,i-\\frac{1}{x{y}^{2}z}\\,j-\\frac{1}{xy{z}^{2}}\\text{ }k. &  & \\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-128529" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The gradient of the product of two functions $f(x,y)$ and $h(x,y)$ is given by\n\n$$\n∇[fh]=h∇f+f∇h.\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇[f(x,y,z)h(x,y,z)] & =h(x,y,z)∇f(x,y,z)+f(x,y,z)∇h(x,y,z) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{xyz}({y}^{2}{z}^{3}\\,i+2xy{z}^{3}\\,j+3x{y}^{2}{z}^{2}\\,k)+x{y}^{2}{z}^{3}(-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}yz}\\,i-\\frac{1}{x{y}^{2}z}\\,j-\\frac{1}{xy{z}^{2}}\\,k) \\\\  & =\\frac{{y}^{2}{z}^{3}}{xyz}\\,i+\\frac{2xy{z}^{3}}{xyz}\\,j+\\frac{3x{y}^{2}{z}^{2}}{xyz}\\,k-\\frac{x{y}^{2}{z}^{3}}{{x}^{2}yz}\\,i-\\frac{x{y}^{2}{z}^{3}}{x{y}^{2}z}\\,j-\\frac{x{y}^{2}{z}^{3}}{xy{z}^{2}}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{y{z}^{2}}{x}\\,i+2{z}^{2}\\,j+3yz\\,k-\\frac{y{z}^{2}}{x}\\,i-{z}^{2}\\,j-yz\\,k \\\\  & ={z}^{2}\\,j+2yz\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-128529" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "868401a7f37e42bd10de04419ec5ed8ed954a846d1b4a3b0a48d8334dfc0160d"} {"question" "q-128529" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-128529" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3x\\,i+{y}^{2}\\,j-2xy\\,k"] ["math" "x\\,i-2xz\\,k"] ["math" "x\\,i-{z}^{2}\\,j-2yz\\,k"] ["math" "{y}^{2}\\,i+3xy\\,k"] ["math" "{z}^{2}\\,j+2yz\\,k"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "q-128529" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{z}^{2}\\,j+2yz\\,k"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/state.json" "file_sha256" "3acd1775ceea7b0c6541ba6db0e5a9c2350b87f4522ae15eb4031f985d5bd748"} {"question" "e-3131" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $\\nabla f(x,y)$ at the point $(1,\\pi)$ given that $f(x,y) = (x - y)\\cos y.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/example-3131.json" "file_sha256" "255e9d20c16a187465a37cd23af4b10fdcddc4063e08648ca8f929bfe20c94b3"} {"question" "e-3131" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the partial derivatives: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}((x-y)\\operatorname{cos}⁡y) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡y \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}((x-y)\\operatorname{cos}⁡y) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-(x-y)\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\text{ }i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\text{ }j \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\text{ }i-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+(x-y)\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)\\text{ }j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the gradient at the specified point, we substitute $(x,y)= (1,\\pi)$ into the above, which gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(1,\\pi ) & ={f}_{x}(1,\\pi )\\text{ }i+{f}_{y}(1,\\pi )\\text{ }j \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi \\text{ }i-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi +(1-\\pi )\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi )\\text{ }j \\\\  & =-i+j.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/example-3131.json" "file_sha256" "255e9d20c16a187465a37cd23af4b10fdcddc4063e08648ca8f929bfe20c94b3"} {"question" "e-3132" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate $\\nabla g(x,y,z)$   at $(2,-1,3)$ if $g(x,y,z) = x^2 + xyz.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/example-3132.json" "file_sha256" "6e7a35e7c60584f4a22471b63ef1601364c3bcc89945bdf262f42b7d4703a287"} {"question" "e-3132" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{x}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+xyz) \\\\  & =2x+yz \\\\ {g}_{y}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+xyz) \\\\  & =0+xz \\\\  & =xz \\\\ {g}_{z}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}+xyz) \\\\  & =0+xy \\\\  & =xy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇g(x,y,z) & ={g}_{x}(x,y,z)\\text{ }i+{g}_{y}(x,y,z)\\text{ }j+{g}_{z}(x,y,z)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =(2x+yz)\\text{ }i+(xz)\\text{ }j+(xy)\\text{ }k \\\\ ∇g(2,-1,3) & =(2(2)+(-1)(3))\\text{ }i+2(3)\\text{ }j+2(-1)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =1\\text{ }i+6\\text{ }j-2\\text{ }k \\\\  & =i+6\\text{ }j-2\\text{ }k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/example-3132.json" "file_sha256" "6e7a35e7c60584f4a22471b63ef1601364c3bcc89945bdf262f42b7d4703a287"} {"question" "e-3133" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $f(x,y)= (y-4)\\ln (x-2),$ find the points $(x, y)$ where $\\nabla f(x,y) = \\mathbf 0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/example-3133.json" "file_sha256" "a6beaeaec61c247f237bb7b1f04dae51033dcd475649e64c900d0d2005d52255"} {"question" "e-3133" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the partial derivatives: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}((y-4)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-2)) \\\\  & =\\frac{y-4}{x-2} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}((y-4)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-2)) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\nabla f(x,y) = \\dfrac {y-4}{x-2} \\, \\mathbf i + \\ln(x-2) \\, \\mathbf j.\n$$\n\nNow, we solve $\\nabla f(x,y) = \\mathbf 0\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {y-4}{x-2} \\, \\mathbf i + \\ln(x-2) \\, \\mathbf j = 0 \\  \\mathbf i + 0\\ \\mathbf j\n$$\n\nBy equating the coefficients of $\\mathbf{i}$ on both sides of the equation (and similarly with $\\mathbf{j}$), we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y-4}{x-2}=0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-2)=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get $y-4=0,$ which means $y=4.$  From the second equation, we obtain $\\ln(x-2)=0,$ which means that $x=3.$\n\nTherefore, $\\nabla f(x,y) =\\mathbf  0$ at the point $(3,4).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/example-3133.json" "file_sha256" "a6beaeaec61c247f237bb7b1f04dae51033dcd475649e64c900d0d2005d52255"} {"question" "e-3150" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the gradient of the product $f(x,y) g(x,y)$ given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =xy,\\, &  & ∇f(x,y)=y\\text{ }i+x\\text{ }j, &  &  \\\\ g(x,y) & =\\sqrt{xy},\\, &  & ∇g(x,y)=\\frac{\\sqrt{xy}}{2x}\\text{ }i+\\frac{\\sqrt{xy}}{2y}\\text{ }j. &  & \\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/example-3150.json" "file_sha256" "138b23f48820f526a131807b9028db7709c21c0aee62212293a4ed2c32f98e14"} {"question" "e-3150" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The gradient of the product of two functions $f(x,y)$ and $g(x,y)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\nabla [fg] = g \\, \\nabla\\! f  + f \\, \\nabla\\! g.\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule shown above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇[f(x,y)g(x,y)] & =g(x,y)∇f(x,y)+f(x,y)∇g(x,y) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{xy}(y\\text{ }i+x\\text{ }j)+xy(\\frac{\\sqrt{xy}}{2x}\\text{ }i+\\frac{\\sqrt{xy}}{2y}\\text{ }j) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{xy}(y\\text{ }i+x\\text{ }j)+\\frac{\\sqrt{xy}}{2}(y\\text{ }i+x\\text{ }j) \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{xy}}{2}(y\\text{ }i+x\\text{ }j).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/example-3150.json" "file_sha256" "138b23f48820f526a131807b9028db7709c21c0aee62212293a4ed2c32f98e14"} {"question" "q-36918" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{xyz}}{2}(\\frac{1}{x}\\text{ }i+\\frac{1}{y}\\text{ }j+\\frac{1}{z}\\text{ }k)"] "category" "reviewed_ma_solution" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044185/answer-source-reviews.json" "file_sha256" "1f9e88f3a18b53230bea3a8cdb2a8c47e5e625fa33005f7644bcca265072969b" "reviewer_session" "01a11908-fa8d-7c61-8e03-c1185d0b9506" "rationale" "Where xyz>0, differentiating sqrt(xyz) gives components yz/(2sqrt(xyz)), xz/(2sqrt(xyz)), and xy/(2sqrt(xyz)). These equal sqrt(xyz)/(2x), sqrt(xyz)/(2y), and sqrt(xyz)/(2z), respectively. Thus original option a is correct and agrees with the authentic solution and stored key. Saved grading rejected the submitted option e; this review is a derived judgment rather than a successful grade for option a." "bindings" {"problem" "63e0ffdce133470950dc02de6c2e13c961ee11d5b9347ef19e7c539f18ea534d" "worked_solution" "90b3b826a8c27439094478977412b2e84fb272489ed618eb909fb5cbffa1602d" "original_field" "3b825cbed2995c1aed03cb602ca07e7a7560be447fb64d9c8498e491c686930b" "reviewed_field" "1d0f1a24e479b4ff7756d243dc7c8e6be3ab1f696c60cd17d9890cce1a35961a" "raw_widg